# E §4.1, E §4.2 step 5 (tally 2.1.6, issue #57, the coordinator's pick P4): two plan moves a and ab, one leg each on one
# day into gone after its lifespan, both refused at src. Of several refusals at one place, the first in the typed
# movement order is the one its reads print: a before ab, ids by code point. refcore 2.1.5 booked the legs in their
# text order, `ab|()` before `a|()`, and printed ab.cash (T's g6/refusal_order).
=== m.tally
model ids
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31


source fixture "T's fixture for S's kernel tests (invented values)"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

input amt: money DUK

input d0: date

place src: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place gone: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..2025-01-05

move a: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from src to gone amount amt

move ab: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from src to gone amount amt

ask q: bal(src, 2025-01-31)

version facts
  cite fixture
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 1.00 DUK
  d0 = 2025-01-10
  opening[src] = 500.00 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[gone] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-LIFESPAN a.cash moves into or out of gone outside its lifespan
  cut 2025-12-31
